[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5230451711","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122053#issuecomment-5230451711","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122053","id":5230451711,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN8Jb_w","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T07:52:59Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T08:11:59Z","body":"I took a look at the MRP, and essentially, the problem is that the joint update is called via `call_deferred`, which causes it to occur after `process`.\r\n\r\nThis PR hides the error, but it does not resolve the issue of the joint update being delayed by one frame. The correct approach is to check the `dirty` flag at the beginning of `_process_modification()`, and if it is set, update the joint array immediately; Basically, we just need to call functions like `_update_joints()` in the first line of the `settings` iteration of `_process_modification()`. As long as `_update_joints()` early returns with `dirty == false`, any duplicate cal